## Step 3 — Implement

Apply every constraint in the skill without exception.

> When a task touches multiple categories (e.g. a new end-to-end feature spanning admin UI + server), load **all** matching skills before writing any file.

## Step 4 — Post-Action

After completing the implementation, run any required follow-up:

| What changed | Required action |
|---|---|
| Any `.sql` migration file under `db/migrations/` | `cd apps/server && make migrate-up` **and** update matching `docs/api/consumer/*.md` and/or `docs/api/admin/*.md` in the same PR |
| Any SQL query file under `db/queries/` | `cd apps/server && sqlc generate` |
| New consumer Go handler added | Verify route is registered under `/api/*` in `registerRoutes` in `main.go` |
| New admin Go handler added | Verify route is registered under `/api/admin/*` and the `RequireAdmin` + `Audit` middleware chain applies |
| New component created in `apps/web/` OR `apps/admin/` | Verify against the `component-conventions` **and** `ui-design-system` (New Component) checklists |
| New consumer page added | Verify against the `ui-design-system` New Page (shared) **and** New Web Page checklists (pill primary, consumer-scale typography, mobile-first, Three Hard Responsive Rules) |
| New admin page added | Verify against the `directory-structure-admin` New Module checklist (uses `DataTable` / `FormDrawer` primitives, route registered in `apps/admin/.umirc.ts`) **and** the `ui-design-system` New Page (shared) **and** New Admin Page checklists (renders inside `AdminLayout`, admin-scale typography, Three Hard Responsive Rules, survives 375 px viewport) |
| Mock route removed | Confirm matching service function in `src/services/` is wired up |

